# S,c (large-angle soft) block — minimal synthetic instance showing the
# ACCEPTED maple syntax, for trees where no final-final example survives.
# Every UPPERCASE token is a placeholder; the lowercase letters are FN
# argument letters with this legend:
#   k          the soft parton
#   i, j       the pair whose iterated clusters the SS terms correct
#   l, m       the far hard radiators the true eikonal connects to
# Momenta: [a,b] = once-mapped cluster, [[a,b],c] = twice-mapped.
# The SFF arguments are (radiator, soft, radiator): a difference of
# eikonals between the dipoles the ITERATED product produces and the
# dipole the TRUE ME has — the construction is measured, not copied
# (residue fitter, probe-me-ir-structure mode 3).
#
# This file is a syntax skeleton: replace X30NAME/REDME/JETnm/the
# letters, renumber aN into your term (map_blocks.py), then VERIFY BY
# REGENERATING, not by assertion — see SKILL.md ("S,c wiring at the
# Fortran level") for the regeneration procedure.

FN:=DUMMYTERM(1,2,i,j,k,l,m):

XX:=
# block: Sc
-( SFF(l,k,[j,k]) + SFF([i,k],k,m)
 - SFF(l,k,[k,i]) - SFF([j,k],k,m) )
 *X30NAME(l,[i,k],[j,k])
 *REDME([l,[i,k]],[[i,k],[j,k]],m,1,2)
 *JETnm([l,[i,k]],[[i,k],[j,k]],m)*a1
:
